# Data comparison across representations

Verifies comparisons between integer and decimal measures combine unit scaling with representation promotion. A decimal 1.5KB exceeds an integer 1000B and equals 1500B exactly, and a decimal mebibyte still exceeds a decimal megabyte since the binary unit carries more bits than its decimal namesake.

>>> source
const whole: int = 1000B
const fractional: decimal = 1.5KB
print(fractional > whole)
print(fractional == 1500B)
print(whole < fractional)
const binary: decimal = 1MiB
const decimal_unit: decimal = 1MB
print(binary > decimal_unit)

<<< stdout
true
true
true
true

<<< stderr
